T*
(Python is a modern, high-level, interpreted, dynamically-typed programming language) Tj
T*
(created by Guido van Rossum:) Tj
T*
(* Key Features: Clean readable syntax \(PEP 8 standard\), automatic memory management) Tj
T*
(via garbage collection, dynamically typed \(variables bind to objects, not types\),) Tj
T*
(platform independent \(bytecode compiled to .pyc and executed on CPython Virtual) Tj
T*
(Machine\).) Tj
T*
(* Execution Modes: Interactive Shell \(REPL - Read-Eval-Print Loop\) for rapid) Tj
T*
(prototyping vs Script Mode \(.py files\) for structured engineering software.) Tj
T*
(* Documentation & Comments: Single-line comments starting with #; multi-line) Tj
T*
(documentation strings \(Docstrings\) enclosed in triple quotes \(""" or ''\) accessible) Tj
T*
(via help\(\) and __doc__ attribute.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
