(>> 1.2 Data Types, Dynamic Typing and Variable Memory Model) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Primitive Built-in Types: int \(arbitrary precision integer\), float \(64-bit IEEE 754) Tj
T*
(double precision\), bool \(True or False, subclass of int\), complex \(real + imag*1j\),) Tj
T*
(str \(immutable Unicode sequence\).) Tj
T*
(* Dynamic Typing: Variable names are merely references \(pointers\) to objects in heap) Tj
T*
(memory. Reassigning a variable re-binds the pointer to a new object.) Tj
T*
(* Inspection Utilities: type\(x\) returns object data type; id\(x\) returns unique memory) Tj
T*
(address identity; isinstance\(x, type\) verifies inheritance compatibility.) Tj
T*
(* Type Conversion \(Casting\): Implicit casting \(e.g., int + float automatically) Tj
T*
(promotes to float\) vs Explicit casting using constructor functions \(int\(\), float\(\),) Tj
T*
(str\(\), bool\(\), complex\(\)\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
